1. PROBLEM STATEMENT:
The Flight Booking System is a C++ application developed using a Singly Linked List to manage flight booking records. 
It allows users to book flights, display all bookings, search for a booking using Booking ID, and cancel bookings.
It also demonstrates dynamic memory allocation functions such as malloc(), calloc(), realloc(), and free().

2. Approach
The Flight Booking System uses a Singly Linked List to store and manage flight booking records dynamically. 
Each node contains the booking details and a pointer to the next node. 
The system supports booking, displaying, searching, and cancelling flights. 
It also demonstrates dynamic memory allocation using malloc(), calloc(), realloc(), and free().

3. Complexity Analysis
Operation	          Time Complexity	     Space Complexity

Book / Insert Booking	      0(1)*	               O(1)
Display Bookings	          0(n)	               O(1)
Search Booking	            0(n)	               O(1)
Cancel Booking	            0(n)	               O(1)
Total Linked List Storage	    —	                 O(n)

4. Conclusion

The Flight Booking System was successfully implemented using a Singly Linked List in C++. 
It performs insertion, display, searching, and cancellation of flight bookings. 
The project also demonstrates dynamic memory allocation functions and helps in understanding pointers,
linked-list operations, and memory management.
